From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH 084/100] sagit: emulate userspace LSE atomics in kernel

MSM8998 (Cortex-A73/A53, ARMv8.0) has no LSE atomics and no CRC32.
Userspace binaries for iOS 16 contain LSE instructions; the kernel
traps them as undefined instructions in handle_uncategorized() and
emulates each with an LDXR/STXR loop so atomicity is preserved across
CPUs. Only userspace (EL0) instructions are emulated; the kernel itself
is compiled with -march=armv8-a so it emits no LSE.

Helpers live in osfmk/arm64/sagit_lse_asm.s (auto-generated by macros
for all op x size x ordering combinations). The dispatch table in
sleh.c maps decoded fields to the right helper.
